@@ -130,6 +130,24 @@ The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each hold
 
 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+The clinic also publishes its specialties as a directory in their own right. One page names every specialty the clinic stores, by its stored name, and under each specialty lists the veterinarians who hold it `[REQ-VET-003]`. Each veterinarian is shown by full name with the first name before the last, so Helen Leary reads as "Helen Leary". This page presents specialties, not the full veterinarian roster: a veterinarian holding no specialty appears under no specialty and so is absent from the page. Every specialty renders together on one page, without pagination. The page is reached by its own address. Publishing a navigation entry or a link to it from another page is not part of this capability. The directory stays read-only — managing veterinarians or specialties is out of scope (NG-2).
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's stored specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is named with the veterinarians who hold it, all on one page without pagination.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian who holds a specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown by full name with the first name before the last.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian who holds no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on the page.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A stored specialty that no veterinarian holds is still named, shown with no veterinarians under it.
+2. Specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one, and the veterinarians under each specialty likewise.
+3. When the clinic stores no specialties, the page renders as an empty directory rather than failing.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
 ### Language
 
 <a id="req-lang-001"></a><a id="req-lang-002"></a>
